	abstract = {The introduction of new gesture interfaces has been expanding the possibilities of creating new Digital Musical Instruments (DMIs). Leap Motion Controller was recently launched promising fine-grained hand sensor capabilities. This paper proposes a preliminary study and evaluation of this new sensor for building new DMIs. Here, we list a series of gestures, recognized by the device, which could be theoretically used for playing a large number of musical instruments. Then, we present an analysis of precision and latency of these gestures as well as a first case study integrating Leap Motion with a virtual music keyboard.},
